        "explanation": "Since \\(x\\ne0\\), divide by \\(x^2\\): \\(\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2-5\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)+6=0\\). Thus \\(t=2\\) or \\(3\\). The distinct real solutions are \\(1,\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2},\\frac{3-\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\), whose sum is \\(4\\).",
