        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "If the real solutions of \\((x^2-3x+2)(x^2-3x+4)=3\\) are \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\), then \\(\\alpha+\\beta\\) equals",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let \\(t=x^2-3x+3\\). Then the equation becomes \\((t-1)(t+1)=3\\), so \\(t^2=4\\). Since \\(t=\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}>0\\), we take \\(t=2\\). Thus \\(x^2-3x+1=0\\), and \\(\\alpha+\\beta=3\\).",
