        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "The number of integers satisfying \\( (x^2-4x+1)(x^2-4x-5)\\le 0 \\) is",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let \\(t=x^2-4x\\). Then \\((t+1)(t-5)\\le0\\), so \\(-1\\le t\\le5\\). Since \\(t=(x-2)^2-4\\), we get \\(3\\le(x-2)^2\\le9\\). Hence \\(x\\in[-1,2-\\sqrt3]\\cup[2+\\sqrt3,5]\\), whose integer elements are \\(-1,0,4,5\\). Therefore, the number of integers is \\(4\\).",
